hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-57 = cons "**Forgetting, fibers, and descent.** An observation o : H → O partitions the history space without loss when both reading and compatible history are kept: H ≃ Σ_{y:O} Fib_o(y) (`fiber`, `fiberEquiv`, §1 equation 1.2). Passing to y alone discards the fiber Fib_o(y): the exact conditional uncertainty left open by the channel, with no prior distribution invented to mask it. Whether a law on the whole descends through o is a checkable condition, not an assumption. The paper's two-bit involution (`whole-step-involution`) loses nothing on Bool × Bool, yet `no-observed-law` proves that no autonomous next-state function exists on the observed coordinate alone. Refining an observation shrinks the fiber (`warrants-refine`); a lossy channel widens it." (cons "" nil)
